; S-02 persistent treap operations — kernel/forms/helpers/treap.form
;
; Implements the four treap helpers required by S-02/cap-registry,
; per the spec in kernel/types/Treap.md (post-v0.1.1).
;
; Operations encoded here:
;
;   S-02/treap/lookup                  (TreapRoot, CapId)    → CapEntry | BOTTOM
;   S-02/treap/insert                  (TreapRoot, CapEntry) → TreapRoot
;   S-02/treap/lookup_with_revocation  (TreapRoot, CapId)    → CapEntry | BOTTOM
;   S-02/treap/bump_generation         (TreapRoot, CapId)    → TreapRoot
;
; CONTRACT NOTE (load-bearing — read before changing trap kinds):
;
;   The four operations are TOTAL functions over a well-formed
;   treap. They do NOT trap on a missing or revoked key. This is
;   not a stylistic choice — it is forced by the frozen S-02 Forms
;   that consume them:
;
;     * S-02/attenuate (S-02-cap-registry.form) calls treap/lookup
;       and immediately compares the result against BOTTOM_HASH
;       (`→ CapEntry or BOTTOM`). attenuate's declared-traps is
;       (ENOTHELD ETYPE) — it cannot propagate an EUNHELD from
;       lookup.
;     * S-02/lookup wraps treap/lookup_with_revocation with
;       declared-traps () and RETs the result directly; S-02/holds
;       then compares it against BOTTOM_HASH. A revoked or absent
;       cap must therefore surface as BOTTOM, never as a trap.
;     * S-02/revoke calls treap/bump_generation behind a CAPHELD
;       guard and declares only (ENOTHELD); a held cap is always in
;       the treap, so bump_generation treats the (unreachable)
;       absent branch as the identity rather than trapping.
;
;   kernel/types/Treap.md previously documented EUNHELD-on-miss and a
;   `trap EREVOKED`. EREVOKED is NOT in the IL's closed trap
;   enumeration (kernel/IL.md § Trap kinds — eleven exactly), and the
;   EUNHELD claim contradicted the frozen S-02 body above. Treap.md
;   has been corrected in the same commit that introduced this file;
;   this file is the authority the proof artifacts compose against.
;
; Synthesis chain:
;   provocation:  STUBS.md catalogues four S-02/treap/* helpers as
;                 pending; PR #30 closed the Treap.md spec gap. The
;                 encoding gap is the next step on the path to
;                 v0.2.5-ignis0-store, alongside the trie (PR #32)
;                 and forest (PR #33) batches.
;   grounding:    A0.5 (energy is finite — O(log n) expected depth),
;                 A1.1/A1.4 (content-addressed, shared by reference —
;                 persistence is automatic), A2.3 (revocation cascades
;                 — paid at lookup via the generation chain), A6.1
;                 (code is substance). The canonicity property (two
;                 treaps with the same (CapId → CapEntry) multiset
;                 have the same root hash) is what S-02 obligation 4
;                 ("lookup totality") composes against.
;   approach:     BST on CapId (lexicographic on the 32 hash bytes,
;                 via Treap/key_lt) + max-heap on a key-derived
;                 priority (Treap/derive_priority). Each public Form
;                 reads its TreapRoot, dispatches by type-tag
;                 (Treap/type_tag_is_{empty,branch}), and either
;                 returns (base case) or recurses / delegates the
;                 rotate-up to the Treap/branch_* schema sub-helpers.
;   composes_with:
;                 - kernel/types/Treap.md (the layout spec)
;                 - the encoded S-02/proj/* projections (holder,
;                   generation) for the revocation chain
;                 - the Treap/* and CapEntry/* schema sub-helpers
;                   catalogued as pending in STUBS.md
;
; Helper exemption: each Form below exceeds the ~30-instruction
; smallness threshold of synthesis/PROTOCOL.md § Helper exemption, so
; each ships its own .proof obligation that S-08's walker recurses
; into; this file's footer drafts those obligations. The .proof
; artifact lands as a v0.2.0-helpers follow-up (ROADMAP action item 10),
; the same track as trie.proof / forest.proof.
;
; Pending leaves: every body below delegates to Treap/* and
; CapEntry/* schema sub-helpers that are NOT in this file — they are
; catalogued in STUBS.md and encoded in a subsequent treap-schema
; batch. Until then the treap operations have pending leaves at every
; inner CALL, per the layered convention from trie.form / forest.form.

; ============================================================
; S-02/treap/lookup
;
; BST walk by cap_id. Returns the stored cap_entry hash on hit,
; BOTTOM_HASH on miss (see CONTRACT NOTE).
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   lookup(root_h, cap_id):
;     node = read(root_h)
;     if type(node) == "TreapEmpty/v1": return BOTTOM_HASH
;     node_key = node.cap_id
;     if node_key == cap_id: return node.cap_entry
;     if cap_id < node_key:  return lookup(node.left,  cap_id)
;     else:                  return lookup(node.right, cap_id)
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "treap_lookup"
  :declared-caps (S-02/TREAP_RO)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE)
  :arity         2
  :locals-n      6
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h (TreapRoot)
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := cap_id (CapId)

    LOAD    0
    READ
    STORE   2                            ; locals[2] := node bytes

    ;; Empty ⇒ miss.
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "Treap/type_tag_is_empty"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1
    JMPZ    +lk_branch
    PUSH    BOTTOM_HASH
    RET

    :lk_branch
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "TreapBranch/proj/cap_id"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1
    STORE   3                            ; locals[3] := node_key

    ;; Key match ⇒ return this node's cap_entry.
    LOAD    3
    LOAD    1
    EQ
    JMPZ    +lk_descend
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "TreapBranch/proj/cap_entry"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1
    RET

    :lk_descend
    ;; cap_id < node_key ⇒ go left, else go right.
    LOAD    1
    LOAD    3
    PUSH    "Treap/key_lt"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → (cap_id < node_key)?
    JMPZ    +lk_right

    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "TreapBranch/proj/left"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → left subtree hash
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "S-02/treap/lookup"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; tail call
    RET

    :lk_right
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "TreapBranch/proj/right"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → right subtree hash
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "S-02/treap/lookup"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; tail call
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/treap-rationale
)

; ============================================================
; S-02/treap/insert
;
; BST-inserts (cap_id, cap_entry) by key, then rotates up until
; the heap property is restored. At mint time cap_id == the
; CapEntry's content hash, so the single Hash argument serves as
; both the BST key and the initial value (Treap.md § insert; this
; is exactly how S-02/attenuate calls it). If cap_id is already
; present the new entry replaces the old one.
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   insert(root_h, entry_h):
;     prio = Treap/derive_priority(entry_h)
;     node = read(root_h)
;     if type(node) == "TreapEmpty/v1":
;         return Treap/seal_leaf_branch(entry_h, prio, entry_h)
;     ; Branch: BST descent + rotate-up handled by the sub-helper,
;     ; which recurses through S-02/treap/insert on the chosen child.
;     return Treap/branch_insert(node, entry_h)
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "treap_insert"
  :declared-caps (S-02/TREAP_RW)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE EBADLOCAL)
  :arity         2
  :locals-n      6
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := entry_h (== cap_id at mint)

    LOAD    0
    READ
    STORE   2                            ; locals[2] := node bytes

    ;; Empty ⇒ seal a singleton branch (left = right = EMPTY_TREAP).
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "Treap/type_tag_is_empty"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1
    JMPZ    +ins_branch

    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Treap/derive_priority"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → priority (Nat)
    STORE   3
    LOAD    1                            ; entry_h (cap_id)
    LOAD    3                            ; priority
    LOAD    1                            ; cap_entry (== entry_h)
    PUSH    "Treap/seal_leaf_branch"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=3                     ; → singleton TreapRoot
    RET

    :ins_branch
    ;; Branch — Treap/branch_insert does the BST descent, recurses
    ;; via S-02/treap/insert, and rotates up to restore the heap.
    LOAD    2
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Treap/branch_insert"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → rebuilt TreapRoot
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/treap-rationale
)

; ============================================================
; S-02/treap/lookup_with_revocation
;
; The contract S-02/lookup → S-02/holds composes against. First a
; plain BST lookup; if that misses, BOTTOM. Otherwise walk the
; cap's derivation chain (via CapEntry.parent) re-doing a lookup
; on each ancestor and comparing the stored generation against the
; value the child recorded at attenuation time. If any ancestor's
; stored generation is higher than the recorded one the cap is
; revoked ⇒ BOTTOM. Otherwise the matched cap_entry.
;
; The chain walk is bounded by the cap's derivation depth (S-02
; obligation 2, "attenuation monotonicity") and lives in
; Treap/check_revocation_chain, which returns the entry hash or
; BOTTOM_HASH — never traps.
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   lwr(root_h, cap_id):
;     entry_h = lookup(root_h, cap_id)
;     if entry_h == BOTTOM_HASH: return BOTTOM_HASH
;     return Treap/check_revocation_chain(root_h, cap_id, entry_h)
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "treap_lookup_with_revocation"
  :declared-caps (S-02/TREAP_RO)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE)
  :arity         2
  :locals-n      6
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := cap_id

    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "S-02/treap/lookup"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → entry_h or BOTTOM
    STORE   2

    ;; Miss ⇒ BOTTOM.
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    BOTTOM_HASH
    EQ
    JMPZ    +lwr_chain
    PUSH    BOTTOM_HASH
    RET

    :lwr_chain
    ;; Present — verify no ancestor has revoked it.
    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "Treap/check_revocation_chain"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=3                     ; → entry_h (live) or BOTTOM (revoked)
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/treap-rationale
)

; ============================================================
; S-02/treap/bump_generation
;
; Locates the entry for cap_id, produces a new CapEntry/v1 with
; generation += 1, and re-inserts it over the old one (same cap_id,
; in-place replacement preserving tree shape). Returns the new
; root. This is how S-02/revoke propagates revocation in O(log n).
;
; Absent branch: the sole caller (S-02/revoke) guards with CAPHELD,
; so a held cap is always present; the absent branch is the
; identity (returns the root unchanged) rather than a trap — see
; CONTRACT NOTE above.
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   bump(root_h, cap_id):
;     node = read(root_h)
;     if type(node) == "TreapEmpty/v1": return root_h    ; unreachable for held cap
;     node_key = node.cap_id
;     if node_key == cap_id:
;         new_entry   = CapEntry/with_generation_inc(read-via node.cap_entry)
;         new_entry_h = Treap/seal_entry(new_entry)
;         return Treap/branch_replace_entry(node, new_entry_h)
;     if cap_id < node_key: return branch with left  := bump(node.left,  cap_id)
;     else:                 return branch with right := bump(node.right, cap_id)
;
; The descent + rebuild for the recursive cases is delegated to
; Treap/branch_bump_generation, which recurses through
; S-02/treap/bump_generation on the chosen child.
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "treap_bump_generation"
  :declared-caps (S-02/TREAP_RW)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE EBADLOCAL)
  :arity         2
  :locals-n      8
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := cap_id

    LOAD    0
    READ
    STORE   2                            ; locals[2] := node bytes

    ;; Empty ⇒ identity (caller guarantees presence).
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "Treap/type_tag_is_empty"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1
    JMPZ    +bg_branch
    LOAD    0
    RET

    :bg_branch
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "TreapBranch/proj/cap_id"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1
    STORE   3                            ; locals[3] := node_key

    ;; Key match ⇒ bump this node's entry generation in place.
    LOAD    3
    LOAD    1
    EQ
    JMPZ    +bg_descend

    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "TreapBranch/proj/cap_entry"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → old cap_entry hash
    READ                                 ; → old CapEntry bytes
    PUSH    "CapEntry/with_generation_inc"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → new CapEntry bytes
    PUSH    "Treap/seal_entry"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → new cap_entry hash
    STORE   4
    LOAD    2
    LOAD    4
    PUSH    "Treap/branch_replace_entry"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → rebuilt TreapRoot
    RET

    :bg_descend
    ;; Recursive case — Treap/branch_bump_generation descends the
    ;; correct child (via key_lt), recurses through
    ;; S-02/treap/bump_generation, and rebuilds the branch. The
    ;; cap_id BST key is unchanged so no rotation is needed.
    LOAD    2
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Treap/branch_bump_generation"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → rebuilt TreapRoot
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/treap-rationale
)

(exports
  (treap_lookup                 (TreapRoot, CapId)    → CapEntry)
  (treap_insert                 (TreapRoot, CapEntry) → TreapRoot)
  (treap_lookup_with_revocation (TreapRoot, CapId)    → CapEntry)
  (treap_bump_generation        (TreapRoot, CapId)    → TreapRoot))

; ============================================================
; Pending sub-helpers introduced by this batch
;
; The bodies above delegate to fifteen new sub-helpers that
; constitute the schema layer for the treap. They are catalogued in
; STUBS.md as pending under the S-02 section and will be encoded in
; the next v0.2.0-helpers batch (treap-schema.form):
;
;   Treap/type_tag_is_empty          (Bytes) → Bool
;   Treap/type_tag_is_branch         (Bytes) → Bool
;   TreapBranch/proj/cap_id          (Bytes) → Hash
;   TreapBranch/proj/cap_entry       (Bytes) → Hash
;   TreapBranch/proj/left            (Bytes) → Hash
;   TreapBranch/proj/right           (Bytes) → Hash
;   Treap/key_lt                     (CapId, CapId) → Bool
;   Treap/derive_priority            (CapId) → Nat
;   Treap/seal_leaf_branch           (CapId, Nat, Hash) → TreapRoot
;   Treap/branch_insert              (Bytes, Hash) → TreapRoot
;   Treap/branch_bump_generation     (Bytes, CapId) → TreapRoot
;   Treap/branch_replace_entry       (Bytes, Hash) → TreapRoot
;   Treap/check_revocation_chain     (TreapRoot, CapId, Hash) → Hash
;   CapEntry/with_generation_inc     (CapEntry) → CapEntry
;   Treap/seal_entry                 (CapEntry) → Hash
;
; Treap/key_lt is the lexicographic comparison of two 32-byte hash
; keys (the IL's LT is Nat-only); Treap/derive_priority recomputes
; `first 8 bytes of BLAKE3(cap_id ‖ "treap-priority")` (Treap.md
; § Priority derivation), and Treap/seal_leaf_branch /
; Treap/branch_* enforce the BST + heap + priority invariants,
; trapping EBADLOCAL on violation (Treap.md § TreapBranch/v1).
; Treap/check_revocation_chain walks CapEntry.parent links using the
; encoded S-02/proj/generation projection.
;
; Until those sub-helpers exist, the four treap operations above
; have pending leaves at every inner CALL, per the layered-encoding
; convention. This file establishes the shape S-02's body sees and
; the .proof artifacts compose against.
; ============================================================

; ============================================================
; Proof obligations (drafted; full discharge in treap.proof)
;
; O1. Totality. lookup / lookup_with_revocation return BOTTOM_HASH
;     (never trap) on a missing or revoked key; bump_generation is
;     the identity on the absent branch. The only declared traps are
;     ETYPE (malformed node bytes) and EBADLOCAL (BST/heap/priority
;     invariant violation, raised inside the Treap/branch_* and
;     Treap/seal_* sub-helpers). This is exactly the contract the
;     frozen S-02 Forms compose against (see CONTRACT NOTE), and it
;     backs S-02 obligation 4 ("lookup totality").
;
; O2. Persistence. No operation mutates an input node substance.
;     Every modification goes through Treap/seal_* (via
;     seal_leaf_branch / seal_entry / branch_*). There is no WRITE or
;     MINT in any body, so a returned root either equals the input
;     root (idempotent / absent branches) or is a freshly sealed
;     tree sharing all untouched subtrees by reference (A1.4).
;
; O3. Canonicity. The treap's shape is fully determined by its key
;     set plus the key-derived priorities (Treap.md § Canonicity
;     proof sketch). insert restores the heap by rotate-up and
;     derive_priority is a pure function of the key, so two treaps
;     holding the same (cap_id → cap_entry) multiset have the same
;     root hash regardless of insertion order. Composes against
;     Treap/branch_insert's "rotate-up restores the max-heap
;     property" obligation.
;
; O4. Revocation monotonicity. bump_generation only ever increases a
;     CapEntry's generation (CapEntry/with_generation_inc adds 1, no
;     other path writes generation) and preserves the cap_id BST key,
;     so the tree shape is unchanged and check_revocation_chain's
;     "stored generation ≥ recorded generation ⇒ revoked" test is
;     monotone in revocation events (A2.3). Backs S-02 obligation 2.
;
; Discharge target: kernel/forms/helpers/treap.proof (non-exempt
; per the helper exemption — sized above the threshold).
; ============================================================
